Please describe the bug 🐞
Description
BigQueryMetastoreClientImpl configures retries for ConnectException and UnknownHostException, but its [exception handler](

      iceberg/bigquery/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/gcp/bigquery/BigQueryMetastoreClientImpl.java

        Lines 114 to 122
      in
      0f3131f

           public static final ExceptionHandler BIGQUERY_EXCEPTION_HANDLER =

               ExceptionHandler.newBuilder()

                   .abortOn(RuntimeException.class)

                   // Retry on connection failures due to transient network issues.

                   .retryOn(java.net.ConnectException.class)

                   // Retry to recover from temporary DNS resolution failures.

                   .retryOn(java.net.UnknownHostException.class)

                   .addInterceptors(EXCEPTION_HANDLER_INTERCEPTOR)

                   .build();

) aborts on RuntimeException. The [exception handler interceptor](

      iceberg/bigquery/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/gcp/bigquery/BigQueryMetastoreClientImpl.java

        Lines 93 to 103
      in
      0f3131f

           @Override

           public RetryResult beforeEval(Exception exception) {

             if (exception instanceof BaseServiceException serviceException) {

               boolean retriable = serviceException.isRetryable();

               return retriable

                   ? ExceptionHandler.Interceptor.RetryResult.RETRY

                   : ExceptionHandler.Interceptor.RetryResult.CONTINUE_EVALUATION;

             }

             return ExceptionHandler.Interceptor.RetryResult.CONTINUE_EVALUATION;

           }

) does not inspect wrapped causes.
Meanwhile, [internalCreate(Table)](https://github.com/apache/iceberg/blob/0f3131f02fc2560bd122f3b323d13ea935892eb3/bigquery/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/gcp/bigquery/BigQueryMetastoreClientImpl.java#L349-L365) catches IOException from the BigQuery table insert and wraps it in RuntimeIOException.
As a result, a transient connection or DNS failure during table creation fails immediately instead of following the configured retry policy.
Expected Behavior
Wrapped ConnectException and UnknownHostException causes should follow the configured retry policy, while unrelated runtime exceptions remain non-retryable.
This report concerns retry classification only; it does not claim that table creation is retried after an ambiguous successful insert.
