Apache Iceberg version
1.12.0 (latest release)
Query engine
Other
Please describe the bug 🐞
On a v3 table with a timestamp_ns column ts partitioned by identity(ts), an IN or NOT IN filter with two or more values fails during scan planning:
table.newScan()
    .filter(Expressions.in("ts", "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000000001", "2025-01-01T00:00:00.000000001"))
    .planFiles();
// java.lang.ArithmeticException: long overflow
For timestamps near 1970-01-01 there is no error, but the results are wrong:

IN skips files that contain matching rows.
newDelete().deleteFromRowFilter(notIn(...)) deletes files whose rows all match an excluded value.

Schema schema = new Schema(optional(1, "ts", Types.TimestampNanoType.withoutZone()));
PartitionSpec spec = PartitionSpec.builderFor(schema).identity("ts").build();
// format v3 table; each case appends one DataFile whose partition is set with
// PartitionData.set(0, DateTimeUtil.isoTimestampToNanos(<its ts>))

// file2026 partitioned at ts = 2026-01-01T00:00:00.000000001
table.newScan().filter(Expressions.in("ts",
    "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000000001", "2025-01-01T00:00:00.000000001")).planFiles();
// before: ArithmeticException: long overflow    after: 1 file

// file1970 partitioned at ts = 1970-01-01T00:00:00.000001
table.newScan().filter(Expressions.in("ts",
    "1970-01-01T00:00:00.000001", "1970-01-01T00:00:00.000002")).planFiles();
// before: 0 files    after: 1 file

table.newDelete().deleteFromRowFilter(Expressions.notIn("ts",
    "1970-01-01T00:00:00.000001", "1970-01-01T00:00:00.000002")).commit();
// before: file1970 is deleted (scan returns 0 files)    after: file1970 is kept (1 file)
