Please describe the bug 🐞
After #17578, Parquet types are validated against the Iceberg type. This is great!
In an attempt to reduce the number of readers that had to consider CRSes or PROJJSON or axis ordering, arrow-rs and Arrow C++ (i.e., the arrow interfaces to Parquet writing) make an attempt to write a defaulted CRS. Unfortunately, this means those interfaces can't currently write Parquet files with "EPSG:4326" as the Geometry or Geography CRS.
arrow-rs: https://github.com/apache/arrow-rs/blob/7dcc1602c460e25a624fd4f095a786352808b884/parquet/src/arrow/schema/extension.rs#L183-L196
arrow C++: https://github.com/apache/arrow-rs/blob/7dcc1602c460e25a624fd4f095a786352808b884/parquet/src/arrow/schema/extension.rs#L183-L196
Notably, iceberg-rust is using this interface. This means that when it writes a table in "EPSG:4326", the Parquet files have Geometry or Geography fields with a defaulted CRS, which iceberg-java reads back as "ogc:crs84", considers un equal, and fails validation. EPSG:4326 is probably the most common thing somebody might type themselves here.
Would it be possible to have the Equals implementations be updated to consider EPSG:4326 and OGC:CRS84 equal to each other?

